So, of course, for this comparison, if we're comparing polyglots and typical individuals, we have to look at the responses at these participants' native language, right? Because otherwise, it's difficult to make comparisons because there will be differences in proficiency. But I can take you, your native speaker of English, and I can take a polyglot, whose native language is also. language, right? And if you look at the neural responses to native language, we find that in hyperpolyglots, the language system looks smaller than the typical individuals, meaning the amount of territory that kind of lights up, quote unquote, in the brain when they process language is smaller, and the regions that respond to language respond less strongly when they process language

