So the system that you use to understand and produce language, so to kind of infer meanings from sequences of words and convert your thoughts into sequences of words, that system is totally separate from music. And this is contra many proposals. And that is now, I think, we and a few other groups have strong evidence that the language regions are just not working at all when you're listening to music, even if it's complex and structured and has all sorts of properties that people argue maybe shared between music and language. But there is some overlap at the lower level auditory processing.

