00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:45.000
try to teach you the skill so that we can interact better, right? It's just a very different, it's a very bad, poorly controlled comparison. And there are some claims that underdeveloped executive abilities early on may be helpful, that maybe interfere later on. There is some claims that babies initially don't have the propensity. So speech is a continuous if we're talking about spoken language, right? there's no boundaries between words. And so kids will kind of hear continuous chunks of speech, sometimes in pretty large chunks.

