maybe you then come up with a more sophisticated code so that you can share your thoughts with one another. But in terms of evidence, yes, it seems that the language system is relatively silent as measured with tools like FMRI, when you engage in playing chess, solving problems, doing math, all sorts of things that you would think would be closely linked to language or relying on linguistic representations and in individuals with severe aphasia,

